        "id": 12380,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-21T17:15:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hey, all! I'm a longtime lurker/ruling reader, but now after reading through the entirety of the wiki Card References page I am tired of being on the sidelines. The Multiverse is just too cool.</p>\n<p>My fiancee and I first played Sentinels at a party late last summer, and I decided it was fun enough to try the base set. Now we own nearly all of them and play two heroes apiece just about every night. It's a minor obsession!</p>\n<p>I am filled with questions about the Multiverse. How did Mister Fixer meet his end and what happened to him immediately thereafter? Has anybody made a list of the characters in and quotes from all known Sentinel Comics issues, by issue? Wouldn't it be awesome if the last expansion had an environment that forced both heroes and villains to work together to defeat it? Does anybody else think of Drax the Destroyer when reading Sky-Scraper quotes? <span class=\"bbcode-s\">How do I change my forum username from the default first half of my email address, assigned when I bought something from the store?</span> <span class=\"bbcode-i\">EDIT: Thanks, Rabit!</span> Clearly, I needed to come to this place. So here I am.</p>\n<p>To the &gt;G guys: you come up with the most wonderful superhero names. Awesome.</p>\n<p>VITAL STATISTICS</p>\n<p>Alter ego day job: Steering spaceships</p>\n<p>Favorite hero: Mister Fixer - no, Tachyon - no, Chrono-Ranger - - -</p>\n<p>Favorite villain: Citizen \"In chess, the pawns go first!\" Dawn. Still.</p>\n<p>Most despised villain: The Matriarch. I prefer <span class=\"bbcode-i\">some</span> hope to accompany my pain.</p>\n<p>Con is: The Freedom Five's consciousnesses uploaded into Wraith's Mega-Computer.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:43:53.993Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
